{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Who am I, that I should go, etc.</b> Meaning: even for a mission that is not contrary to his will, for I am not important enough to speak before a king, and consequently he will not believe in his mission and he will be in danger, for a person has free choice and will. Go and learn from the statement of Samuel (1 Samuel 16:2): ״אֵיךְ אֵלֵךְ וְשָׁמַע שָׁאוּל וַהֲרָגָנִי״, and you will find that a person does not believe in prophecy on account of the quality of lowliness, as stated regarding the prophecy of Amos (Ecclesiastes Rabbah 1:1:2) that his contemporaries disparaged him, etc. Further, <b>that I should bring out, etc.</b> — for this one needs a person great in deeds, that he may merit such great merit, and he feared lest a stumble befall Israel on account of his deficiency of merit — and this stems from humility and lowliness."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:53.459441433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}